What is ChromaDB?

ChromaDB is a vector database. It stores text, embeddings and metadata so that we can retrieve relevant information later.

1. Open app.py and replace the code with this:
import chromadbimport ollama# Create ChromaDB clientclient = chromadb.PersistentClient(path="./chroma_db")# Create collectioncollection = client.get_or_create_collection(    name="sanaatana")# Sample documenttext = "Sanaatana provides pooja materials in Shivamogga."# Generate embeddingresponse = ollama.embeddings(    model="nomic-embed-text",    prompt=text)vector = response["embedding"]# Store in ChromaDBcollection.add(    ids=["doc1"],    documents=[text],    embeddings=[vector])print("Document successfully stored in ChromaDB!")print("Total documents:", collection.count())



